{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-42535" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider $E=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ Find the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-42535" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by swapping the first and the third rows of ${I}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}$ to $A.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-42535" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "51e3ee8f0c640b826998b5a97fb773ca47a42af9225d3392e28814938d2731e6"} {"question" "q-42535" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-42535" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{R}_{1}:=-{R}_{1}"] ["math" "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{3}"] ["math" "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}"] ["math" "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}"] ["math" "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-42535" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-110458" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider $E=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ Find the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-110458" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by multiplying the first row of ${I}_{3}$ by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary \nrow operation ${R}_{1}:=5{R}_{1}$ to $A.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-110458" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "51e3ee8f0c640b826998b5a97fb773ca47a42af9225d3392e28814938d2731e6"} {"question" "q-110458" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-110458" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{R}_{1}:=5{R}_{1}"] ["math" "{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1}"] ["math" "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{2}"] ["math" "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{3}"] ["math" "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-110458" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{1}:=5{R}_{1}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-75109" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ Find the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-75109" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the first row of ${I}_{3}$ and adding $2$ times the third row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}$ to $A.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-75109" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "51e3ee8f0c640b826998b5a97fb773ca47a42af9225d3392e28814938d2731e6"} {"question" "q-75109" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-75109" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{R}_{1}:=2{R}_{1}"] ["math" "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}"] ["math" "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}"] ["math" "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{3}"] ["math" "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-75109" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-110464" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]$ and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ Find the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-110464" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by multiplying the third row of ${I}_{3}$ by $9:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=9{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary \nrow operation ${R}_{3}:=9{R}_{3}$ to $A.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-110464" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "51e3ee8f0c640b826998b5a97fb773ca47a42af9225d3392e28814938d2731e6"} {"question" "q-110464" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-110464" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{R}_{3}:=9{R}_{3}"] ["math" "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+9{R}_{1}"] ["math" "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+9{R}_{2}"] ["math" "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{9}{R}_{1}"] ["math" "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-9{R}_{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-110464" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{3}:=9{R}_{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-32147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider $E=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$\nFind the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-32147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by swapping the first and the second rows of ${I}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary \nrow operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ to $A.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-32147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "51e3ee8f0c640b826998b5a97fb773ca47a42af9225d3392e28814938d2731e6"} {"question" "q-32147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-32147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}"] ["math" "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}"] ["math" "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}"] ["math" "{R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}"] ["math" "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-32147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-32146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-32146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-32146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "51e3ee8f0c640b826998b5a97fb773ca47a42af9225d3392e28814938d2731e6"} {"question" "q-32146" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-32146" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-32146" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-42510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-42510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-42510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "51e3ee8f0c640b826998b5a97fb773ca47a42af9225d3392e28814938d2731e6"} {"question" "q-42510" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/state.json" "file_sha256" "2cf98e5518c90a500e7847bad4c4f231679f4277e1f101deedf640291773eefc"} {"question" "q-42510" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"]] "catego