preserving the other rows. Therefore original option 2 and the stored answer are correct. Right multiplication AE generally performs a different column operation. This is a source-backed derived judgment from the original operation and authentic worked solution. The Incorrect grade concerns submitted option 3, not this reviewed answer."}] "usage" {"e-4732" [] "e-4733" [] "e-4734" [] "q-32128" [] "q-32147" []} "basis" 1988 "retractions" [[17592186134109 :question/problem "Consider $E = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and a $3 \\cdot 3$ matrix $A$.\n\nFind the row operation that, when applied to $A$, is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left."] [17592186134106 :question/problem "Suppose that the elementary row operation $R_{2}:=R_{2} - 3R_{3}$ is applied to a $3 \\cdot 3$ matrix $A$. What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?"] [17592186134106 :question/answer-fields 17592186131082] [17592186133473 :question/problem "Consider $\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$.\nFind the row operation that, when applied to $A$, is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left."] [17592186133473 :question/worked-solution "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the second row of $I$ and adding $7$ times the third row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{2} \\mid:=R_{2} + 7R_{3} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= E\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary\nrow operation\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+7R_3\n$$\n\nto $A$."] [17592186133474 :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation $R_2:=R_2-2R_1$ to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$. What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?"] [17592186133474 :question/worked-solution "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation\n\n$$\nR_2:= R_2-2R_1\n$$\n\nto $A$.\n\nTo find $E$, we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{2} \\mid:=R_{2} - 2R_{1} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= E\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [17592186133475 :question/problem "Suppose we are applying these two elementary row operations, in the given order, to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$:\n$R_2\\leftrightarrow R_3, \\qquad R_1:=6R_1$\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication."] [17592186133475 :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is $R_2\\leftrightarrow R_3$. The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n$I|= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{2} \\mid ↔R_{3}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}; = E_{1}$\n- The second operation is $R_1:=6R_1$. The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n$I|= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{1} \\mid:=6R_{1}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}; = E_{2}$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A$, we multiply by $E_1$ on the left and get $E_1 A$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to $E_1 A$, we multiply by $E_2$ on the left and get $E_2 E_1 A$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186131083 17592186131084 17592186131085 17592186131086 17592186131087 17592186131101 17592186131102 17592186131103 17592186131104 17592186131105] "immutable_fields" [[17592186131082 :answer-field/correct] [17592186131082 :answer-field/id] [17592186131082 :answer-field/key] [17592186131082 :answer-field/type] [17592186131100 :answer-field/correct] [17592186131100 :answer-field/id] [17592186131100 :answer-field/key] [17592186131100 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
